{"id": "EUVD-2026-96396", "enisaUuid": "905ab56b-b79b-398f-8798-1f4088967084", "description": "OpenLIT 2.1.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read other projects' telemetry by supplying a forged x-openlit-project-id header. Attackers who know a victim project id and database config id can query the trace read API to obtain traces including LLM prompts and completions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T18:58:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:08", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/openlit-project-context-read", "https://github.com/openlit/openlit/blob/9938c66638666ca5d3bcb850350faa82e510924b/src/client/src/lib/telemetry-source.ts#L113-L125", "https://github.com/openlit/openlit/blob/9938c66638666ca5d3bcb850350faa82e510924b/src/client/src/middleware/check-auth.ts#L22-L33", "https://github.com/openlit/openlit", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openlit-2.1.0-authorization-bypass-via-x-openlit-project-id-header"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108596", "GHSA-fx43-jvpp-9x44"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "77cb2325-f15c-3885-981e-64f4d135301f", "product": {"name": "openlit", "vendor": {"name": "openlit"}}, "product_version": "2.1.0 \u22642.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4e923a7b-3618-3fc3-a60a-90c39c3d28f2", "vendor": {"name": "openlit"}}], "isExploited": false}